#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/preparations.rst:175
msgid ""
"Using an :doc:`image proxy </deployment-guide/server/image-proxy>` means "
"that all requests for images made by Mattermost clients will go through "
"the proxy instead of contacting third-party servers directly. This helps "
"protect user privacy by preventing third-party servers from tracking who "
"views an image. This also prevents the use of tracking pixels (invisible "
"images that do the same thing without the user even seeing an image)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/preparations.rst:177
msgid ""
"Certain proxy servers also provide a layer of caching which can make "
"loading images faster and more reliable. This caching also helps preserve"
" posts by protecting them from dead images."
msgstr ""

